#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:870 ../../../topics/settings.rst:1008
#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:1428 ../../../topics/settings.rst:1535
#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:1611 ../../../topics/settings.rst:1660
#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:1943
msgid "Default: ``None``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:449
msgid "Import path of a given ``asyncio`` event loop class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:451
msgid ""
"If the asyncio reactor is enabled (see :setting:`TWISTED_REACTOR`) or when :"
"ref:`running Scrapy without a reactor <asyncio-without-reactor>` this "
"setting can be used to specify the asyncio event loop to be used with it. "
"Set the setting to the import path of the desired asyncio event loop class. "
"If the setting is set to ``None`` the default asyncio event loop will be "
"used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:458
msgid ""
"If you are installing the asyncio reactor manually using the :func:`~scrapy."
"utils.reactor.install_reactor` function, you can use the ``event_loop_path`` "
"parameter to indicate the import path of the event loop class to be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:462
msgid ""
"Note that the event loop class must inherit from :class:`asyncio."
"AbstractEventLoop`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:464
msgid ""
"Please be aware that, when using a non-default event loop (either defined "
"via :setting:`ASYNCIO_EVENT_LOOP` or installed with :func:`~scrapy.utils."
"reactor.install_reactor`), Scrapy will call :func:`asyncio.set_event_loop`, "
"which will set the specified event loop as the current loop for the current "
"OS thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:470 ../../../topics/settings.rst:750
#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:761 ../../../topics/settings.rst:783
#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:1896 ../../../topics/settings.rst:2268
#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:2405
msgid "This is a :ref:`reactor setting <reactor-settings>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:475
msgid "AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:479
msgid ""
"The AWS access key used by code that requires access to `Amazon Web "
"services`_, such as the :ref:`S3 feed storage backend <topics-feed-storage-"
"s3>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:485
msgid "AWS_ENDPOINT_URL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:489
msgid "Endpoint URL used for S3-like storage, for example Minio or s3.scality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:494
msgid "AWS_MAX_POOL_CONNECTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:500
msgid ""
"Maximum number of connections that AWS clients, such as those of the :ref:"
"`S3 feed storage backend <topics-feed-storage-s3>` and of the :ref:`S3 media "
"pipeline storage backend <media-pipelines-s3>`, keep in their connection "
"pool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:505
msgid ""
"If ``None``, the value of :setting:`REACTOR_THREADPOOL_MAXSIZE` is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:507
msgid ""
"Values lower than the number of parallel AWS calls do not limit those calls, "
"but their connections are closed instead of reused, which hurts performance, "
"and ``Connection pool is full, discarding connection`` warnings are logged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../topics/settings.rst:514
msgid "AWS_REGION_NAME"
msgstr ""

